  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Arya rows at a speed of 7 metres per second in still water. Water is flowing downstream at a constant speed. Arya rows 120 metres downstream then returns 120 metres upstream. Her round trip takes 42 seconds. Find $s$, the speed of the water.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$s=3\\text{ m/s}$.\n\nAdd the downstream and upstream journey times, clear denominators and take the positive root.",
      "worked": "The downstream speed is $7+s$ m/s and the upstream speed is $7-s$ m/s, so $0<s<7$. Using time $=\\text{distance}\\div\\text{speed}$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{120}{7+s}+\\frac{120}{7-s}&=42\\\\120(7-s)+120(7+s)&=42(7+s)(7-s)\\\\1680&=42(49-s^2)\\\\40&=49-s^2\\\\s^2-9&=0\\\\(s-3)(s+3)&=0\\\\s&=3\\text{ or }-3\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $0<s<7$, the water’s speed is $3\\text{ m/s}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
